---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { contactBasics } from '../data/servicePages';

// TODO: fill in before going live (controller details required by GDPR Art. 13)
const controller = {
  legalName: '', // e.g. 'Example Ltd' or full name of the owner
  address: '',   // e.g. 'Street 1, 3000 Limassol, Cyprus'
  registration: '', // e.g. 'Registration No. HE 123456, VAT CY12345678X' (optional)
};

const lastUpdated = '18 November 2026';
const canonical = 'https://ai-cyp.com/privacy-policy/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | AI Automation Cyprus"
  description="How AI Automation Cyprus collects, uses and protects personal data when you visit ai-cyp.com or contact us."
  canonical={canonical}
  robots="noindex, follow"
>

  <div class="post-hero">
    <div class="post-hero-inner">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="post-meta"><span>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="post-content-section">
    <div class="post-content">

      <p>This policy explains what personal data we collect when you visit ai-cyp.com or get in touch with us, why we collect it, and what rights you have. We process personal data in line with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Cyprus Law 125(I)/2018.</p>

      <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        The controller responsible for your personal data is:<br />
        {controller.legalName ? <>{controller.legalName}<br />trading as AI Automation Cyprus<br /></> : <>AI Automation Cyprus<br /></>}
        {controller.address ? controller.address : 'Cyprus'}<br />
        {controller.registration && <>{controller.registration}<br /></>}
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${contactBasics.email}`}>{contactBasics.email}</a><br />
        Phone: <a href={`tel:${contactBasics.phoneHref}`}>{contactBasics.phone}</a>
      </p>
      <p>We have not appointed a Data Protection Officer, as we are not required to. For any privacy question, use the contact details above.</p>

      <h2>2. Visiting the website</h2>
      <p>Our website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you open a page, your browser automatically sends technical data to the server, including your IP address, the date and time of the request, the page requested, the referring page, and your browser and operating system. GitHub may log this data for security purposes and to keep the service running.</p>
      <p>We use this data only to deliver the website securely and reliably. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in operating a secure website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). We do not combine this data with other sources or use it to identify you. More information: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.</p>

      <h2>3. Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>Our website does not set cookies and does not use analytics, advertising or tracking tools. We do not create user profiles.</p>

      <h2>4. Fonts</h2>
      <p>To display text consistently, our website loads fonts from Google Fonts, a service of Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. When a page loads, your browser connects to Google's servers, which transmits your IP address to Google. Google may also process this data in the USA. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a consistent and readable presentation of the website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). More information: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>5. Contact form</h2>
      <p>When you send us a message through the contact form, we collect your name, email address, company name (optional), your message, and the page from which you sent the form. We use this data only to answer your enquiry and, if you wish, to prepare an offer.</p>
      <p>The form is processed by Formspree, a service of Formspree, Inc., USA, which receives the submission and forwards it to us by email. Formspree stores submissions on its servers and may use spam protection tools to block automated abuse. More information: <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Formspree Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      <p>The legal basis is the handling of your request before a possible contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Providing the data is voluntary, but we cannot reply without your name and email address.</p>

      <h2>6. Email, phone and WhatsApp</h2>
      <p>If you contact us by email, phone or WhatsApp, we process the details you share (such as your name, contact details and the content of your message) to answer your request, on the same legal basis as above. If you use WhatsApp, WhatsApp Ireland Limited also processes your data under its own privacy policy.</p>

      <h2>7. How long we keep your data</h2>
      <p>We delete enquiries once they have been fully dealt with and there is no further need to keep them, usually within 12 months of our last contact. If your enquiry leads to a contract, we keep the related records for as long as the law requires, for example under Cyprus tax and accounting rules.</p>

      <h2>8. Who receives your data</h2>
      <p>We share your data only with the service providers named in this policy, who process it on our behalf or as independent providers, and with authorities where the law requires it. We do not sell your data.</p>

      <h2>9. Transfers outside the EU</h2>
      <p>Some of the providers named above are based in the USA or may process data there. Where data is transferred outside the European Economic Area, it is protected by an adequacy decision of the European Commission (such as the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, where the provider is certified) or by the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

      <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15)</li>
        <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16)</li>
        <li>have your data deleted (Art. 17)</li>
        <li>restrict how we process your data (Art. 18)</li>
        <li>receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20)</li>
        <li>object to processing based on our legitimate interests (Art. 21)</li>
        <li>withdraw any consent you have given, with effect for the future (Art. 7(3))</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, email us at <a href={`mailto:${contactBasics.email}`}>{contactBasics.email}</a>.</p>
      <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. In Cyprus this is the Commissioner for Personal Data Protection, Iasonos 1, 1082 Nicosia, <a href="https://www.dataprotection.gov.cy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.dataprotection.gov.cy</a>.</p>

      <h2>11. Automated decisions</h2>
      <p>We do not use automated decision-making or profiling that has legal or similarly significant effects on you.</p>

      <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy when our website or services change, or when the law requires it. The current version is always available on this page.</p>

    </div>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
